## `src/range.ts`

`overlaps` now:

- **Touching ranges don't overlap.** The old code used `aStart <= bEnd && bStart <= aEnd`, which treated an end boundary as inclusive. Since the end is exclusive, I changed the comparison to strict `<` (`aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd`).
- **Same start instant does overlap** — two ranges starting together share an instant, covered by the strict comparisons.
- **Zero-length ranges overlap nothing, not even themselves.** A range whose start equals its end contains no moments, so I return `false` early when either side has zero length.
- **Unparseable dates throw a `TypeError`** whose message includes the offending value (`parseInstant` wraps `Date.parse` and throws when it's `NaN`).
- **End-before-start throws a `RangeError`** naming the offending start/end values, checked for both ranges.
- All four endpoints are parsed before validation, so an unparseable value anywhere throws regardless of ordering.

## `src/range.test.ts`

Added tests for: touching ranges, same-start-instant overlap, containment, zero-length (against itself and against a normal range, both orientations), unparseable dates in each of the four positions (checking the message names the value), and end-before-start for both ranges.

